{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2izmedq3EVLt4geaJ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X5kRBZwx62TEwkr8VZikTw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183530__xf7f297/work/ref/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; cat README.md; ls -la game docs kits modules tools src | head -120; wc -c my-3d2dge.js index.html"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_read_input_tokens":26970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":752},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"d30cb38b-b23f-461f-8bf9-932a4066cdd5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:16.791Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2izVmQS1CWRVbPN1BQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01X5kRBZwx62TEwkr8VZikTw":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183530__xf7f297/work/ref/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; cat README.md; ls -la game docs kits modules tools src | head -120; wc -c my-3d2dge.js index.html"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X5kRBZwx62TEwkr8VZikTw","type":"tool_result","content":"# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.85.2)\n\nEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\nfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n\n**The engine is yours to change.** This copy is yours to fix, extend or rewrite in any way you see fit: `my-3d2dge.js`\nis the engine, readable, with every module, and every page and test here loads it (`modules/` and `my-3d2dge-agent.js`\nare separate copies). If you hand the game back, a line on what you changed and why helps: it shows what the engine\nlacks.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n   `game/` and make it yours.\n3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n   before you use it.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n\nNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\nengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n\n## Run, test, check\n\n```sh\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\nthe two scripts into the page.\n\n## Testing a game without a browser\n\n`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped.\n\n- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n\nThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\ndocs:\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 11643 Nov  3 18:36 ASSETS.md\n\ngame:\ntotal 28\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha 4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha 4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 9122 Nov  3 18:36 game.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1397 Nov  3 18:36 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 2609 Nov  3 18:36 test.mjs\n\nkits:\ntotal 1468\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha   4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha   4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   6980 Nov  3 18:36 README.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1457 Nov  3 18:36 adventure.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  71665 Nov  3 18:36 adventure.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1461 Nov  3 18:36 animlab.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  54246 Nov  3 18:36 animlab.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1392 Nov  3 18:36 arcade.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  74410 Nov  3 18:36 arcade.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1401 Nov  3 18:36 artillery.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  53238 Nov  3 18:36 artillery.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1449 Nov  3 18:36 brawler.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  78902 Nov  3 18:36 brawler.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1398 Nov  3 18:36 fighting.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  36909 Nov  3 18:36 fighting.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1386 Nov  3 18:36 kart.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  35762 Nov  3 18:36 kart.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1410 Nov  3 18:36 metroidvania.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  86459 Nov  3 18:36 metroidvania.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1395 Nov  3 18:36 pinball.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  51523 Nov  3 18:36 pinball.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1461 Nov  3 18:36 platformer.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  79504 Nov  3 18:36 platformer.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1414 Nov  3 18:36 pointclick.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  66846 Nov  3 18:36 pointclick.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1392 Nov  3 18:36 puzzle.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  45272 Nov  3 18:36 puzzle.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1392 Nov  3 18:36 rhythm.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  36633 Nov  3 18:36 rhythm.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1386 Nov  3 18:36 road.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  34669 Nov  3 18:36 road.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1401 Nov  3 18:36 roguelike.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  40240 Nov  3 18:36 roguelike.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1433 Nov  3 18:36 rpg.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 141060 Nov  3 18:36 rpg.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1383 Nov  3 18:36 rts.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  48382 Nov  3 18:36 rts.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1449 Nov  3 18:36 shooter.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 110383 Nov  3 18:36 shooter.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1383 Nov  3 18:36 sim.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  52920 Nov  3 18:36 sim.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1392 Nov  3 18:36 sports.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  50211 Nov  3 18:36 sports.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1449 Nov  3 18:36 stealth.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  37126 Nov  3 18:36 stealth.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1395 Nov  3 18:36 tactics.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  61120 Nov  3 18:36 tactics.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   2244 Nov  3 18:36 test.mjs\n\nmodules:\ntotal 380\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 16107 Nov  3 18:36 arcade.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33195 Nov  3 18:36 click.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 19197 Nov  3 18:36 drive.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 44576 Nov  3 18:36 fight.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 13450 Nov  3 18:36 gen.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 30487 Nov  3 18:36 grid.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 16228 Nov  3 18:36 mode7.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 31868 Nov  3 18:36 physics.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 15431 Nov  3 18:36 rhythm.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 12540 Nov  3 18:36 road.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 15209 Nov  3 18:36 rooms.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 25133 Nov  3 18:36 rpg.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 15749 Nov  3 18:36 songs.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 13969 Nov  3 18:36 story.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 35521 Nov  3 18:36 strategy.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 14361 Nov  3 18:36 terrain.js\n\nsrc:\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha 4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha 4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha 4096 Nov  3 18:36 assets\n\ntools:\ntotal 92\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  4005 Nov  3 18:36 asset-find.mjs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 15817 Nov  3 18:36 asset-lib.mjs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  5499 Nov  3 18:36 asset-set.mjs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 16951 Nov  3 18:36 asset-sheet.mjs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 10145 Nov  3 18:36 check.mjs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 12019 Nov  3 18:36 filmstrip.mjs\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 11199 Nov  3 18:36 replay.mjs\n1234180 my-3d2dge.js\n   6981 index.html\n1241161 total","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"8f033839-88ed-40a0-b49c-e1f1753b4dc6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:16.813Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.85.2)\n\nEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\nfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n\n**The engine is yours to change.** This copy is yours to fix, extend or rewrite in any way you see fit: `my-3d2dge.js`\nis the engine, readable, with every module, and every page and test here loads it (`modules/` and `my-3d2dge-agent.js`\nare separate copies). If you hand the game back, a line on what you changed and why helps: it shows what the engine\nlacks.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n   `game/` and make it yours.\n3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n   before you use it.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n\nNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\nengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n\n## Run, test, check\n\n```sh\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\nthe two scripts into the page.\n\n## Testing a game without a browser\n\n`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped.\n\n- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n\nThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\ndocs:\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 11643 Nov  3 18:36 ASSETS.md\n\ngame:\ntotal 28\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha 4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha 4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 9122 Nov  3 18:36 game.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1397 Nov  3 18:36 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 2609 Nov  3 18:36 test.mjs\n\nkits:\ntotal 1468\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha   4096 Nov  3 18:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 micha micha   4096 Nov  3 18:36 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   6980 Nov  3 18:36 README.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1457 Nov  3 18:36 adventure.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  71665 Nov  3 18:36 adventure.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1461 Nov  3 18:36 animlab.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  54246 Nov  3 18:36 animlab.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1392 Nov  3 18:36 arcade.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  74410 Nov  3 18:36 arcade.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1401 Nov  3 18:36 artillery.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  53238 Nov  3 18:36 artillery.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1449 Nov  3 18:36 brawler.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  78902 Nov  3 18:36 brawler.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1398 Nov  3 18:36 fighting.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  36909 Nov  3 18:36 fighting.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1386 Nov  3 18:36 kart.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  35762 Nov  3 18:36 kart.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1410 Nov  3 18:36 metroidvania.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  86459 Nov  3 18:36 metroidvania.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1395 Nov  3 18:36 pinball.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  51523 Nov  3 18:36 pinball.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1461 Nov  3 18:36 platformer.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  79504 Nov  3 18:36 platformer.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1414 Nov  3 18:36 pointclick.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  66846 Nov  3 18:36 pointclick.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   1392 Nov 