{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGCKpYcAHsfsdSoDJPx5Qx","type":"tool_result","content":"79:- 961 17c. Mover; E.Mover: mover\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n96:- 1430 Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js); E.Fog: fog, E.Grid: grid, E.GridMover: gridmover, E.Turns: turns\n187:- `E.targets(from, list, o = {})`: the things in list that `from` can reach, nearest first, each as { target, d (ground distance), dz, angle (from -> it) }: melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle around facing, radians; default all round), facing (default from.facing), dz (most height difference, default E.HEIGHTS.level), sight: map (only those its\n741:- `map.arcClear(a, b, apex = 20, r = 0)`: does a jump arc from a to b (feet, { x, y, z }) clear every top on the way? The arc is a parabola peaking apex above the higher end; r > 0 also checks a track on each side of it. Jumps, throws, aerial takedowns\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather th\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leap\n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n946:- `action.otherState(extra)` †: the rig state for the other body of a paired action (the victim of a takedown)\n961:## 17c. Mover\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n964:- `mover.dodge(dir, dist = 34)` †: a dodge roll toward dir (an angle or [dx, dy]; default its facing) when it stands free. Returns the action, or null\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n966:- `mover.respawn()` †: back to the last safe spot (after water, a pit, a fall it shouldn't survive)\n967:- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n969:- `mover.accel = 700`, `mover.airAccel = 260` †: how fast it gets there\n970:- `mover.action = null` †: the E.Action playing, or null\n971:- `mover.buffer = .12` †: seconds a jump press is kept\n972:- `mover.climb = true` †: climbs ledges (true)\n973:- `mover.climbAny = false` †: climbs any wall face (see the section's header)\n974:- `mover.climbMax = 82` †: the highest ledge it climbs\n975:- `mover.climbSpeed = 34` †: its climbing speed\n976:- `mover.coyote = .1` †: seconds a jump still works after leaving an edge\n977:- `mover.crouch = false` †: sneaking (a toggle)\n978:- `mover.exhausted = false` †: out of stamina until a third is back\n979:- `mover.facing = 0` †: the angle it faces\n980:- `mover.fell = 0`, `mover.hurt = false`, `mover.inHazard = false` †: what happened this step\n981:- `mover.gapAssist = true` †: a jump at a gap aims for the far side\n982:- `mover.glide = false` †: opens a glide in the air (see the header)\n983:- `mover.glideMin = 24`, `mover.glideSink = 26`, `mover.glideSpeed = 72` †: how high over the ground it opens, how fast it sinks and flies\n984:- `mover.gliding = false` †: gliding now\n985:- `mover.hopMax = 48` †: drops up to this deep are hopped down\n986:- `mover.hurtAt = 72`, `mover.rollAt = 26` †: fall heights that roll and that hurt\n987:- `mover.jumpSpeed = 220` †: a jump's upward speed\n988:- `mover.lastSafe = null` †: the last spot it stood safely, for respawn()\n989:- `mover.lift = 0` †: an updraft's rising speed (a number, or a function of the mover)\n990:- `mover.run = 85`, `mover.sneak = 32`, `mover.sprintSpeed = 125`, `mover.walk = 50` †: top speeds (world units a second)\n991:- `mover.sprinting = false` †: sprinting now\n992:- `mover.stamina` †: what is left (full to start)\n993:- `mover.staminaMax = 0` †: its stamina (0: none)\n994:- `mover.staminaRegen = 35` †: refilled a second standing\n995:- `mover.tire` †: { climb, climbJump, glide, sprint } it costs\n996:- `mover.turn = 14` †: how fast it turns, radians a second\n997:- `mover.vault = 14` †: walls up to this high are vaulted at a run\n998:- `mover.wall = null` †: the face it holds on to (map.wall's), or null\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target se\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1004:- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1006:- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n1007:- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n1008:- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n1009:- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n1010:- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n1011:- `suspicion.level = 0` †: 0..1.2, how suspicious\n1012:- `suspicion.since = 0` †: seconds since it last saw or heard anything\n1013:- `suspicion.state = 'calm'` †: 'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'\n1014:- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (de\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.2</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"157e23a3-583b-4b06-bdb4-2e71f0c6829a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:36.244Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"79:- 961 17c. Mover; E.Mover: mover\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n96:- 1430 Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js); E.Fog: fog, E.Grid: grid, E.GridMover: gridmover, E.Turns: turns\n187:- `E.targets(from, list, o = {})`: the things in list that `from` can reach, nearest first, each as { target, d (ground distance), dz, angle (from -> it) }: melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle around facing, radians; default all round), facing (default from.facing), dz (most height difference, default E.HEIGHTS.level), sight: map (only those its\n741:- `map.arcClear(a, b, apex = 20, r = 0)`: does a jump arc from a to b (feet, { x, y, z }) clear every top on the way? The arc is a parabola peaking apex above the higher end; r > 0 also checks a track on each side of it. Jumps, throws, aerial takedowns\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather th\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leap\n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n946:- `action.otherState(extra)` †: the rig state for the other