{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DmdF1H5mxysfCdHgSkdSHC","type":"tool_result","content":"283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', a\n274:- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K block, L dodge, Q use, M map. Pad: A\n320:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, rig\n47: *    new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit, saves } }), or leave them out (menu: false, fullscreen: false,\n871:   *  gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } }) */\n2962: *      new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }] } }) and reads game.settings.hints.\n3802: *    new E.Game({ menu: { saves: true } }) puts Save (while saves.canSave: a JRPG sets it at a save point) and Load in\n3805: *    menu: { saves: { slots: 3, version: 2, migrate(data, from) { ...; return data; } } } sets them.\n3911:HOOKS.pause = (sh, acts) => {   // the pause menu's Save and Load, with menu: { saves }\n9108: *    defaults). new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [...], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill:\n765:     *  and '' without one); lastDevice: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the\n767:    this.deadzone = .18; this.padIndex = null; this.padId = ''; this.lastDevice = 'keyboard';\n827:      if (e.pointerType !== 'mouse') this.lastDevice = 'touch';   // any touch, on the stick's half or not: prompts follow it\n912:  label(a, device = this.lastDevice) {\n998:    if (code.startsWith('Pad')) { this.lastDevice = 'gamepad'; this.aimSource = 'pad'; }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"792c5005-9c88-45d5-b9b1-530bc1127c10","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:40.707Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', a\n274:- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K block, L dodge, Q use, M map. Pad: A\n320:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, rig\n47: *    new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit, saves } }), or leave them out (menu: false, fullscreen: false,\n871:   *  gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } }) */\n2962: *      new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }] } }) and reads game.settings.hints.\n3802: *    new E.Game({ menu: { saves: true } }) puts Save (while saves.canSave: a JRPG sets it at a save point) and Load in\n3805: *    menu: { saves: { slots: 3, version: 2, migrate(data, from) { ...; return data; } } } sets them.\n3911:HOOKS.pause = (sh, acts) => {   // the pause menu's Save and Load, with menu: { saves }\n9108: *    defaults). new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [...], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill:\n765:     *  and '' without one); lastDevice: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the\n767:    this.deadzone = .18; this.padIndex = null; this.padId = ''; this.lastDevice = 'keyboard';\n827:      if (e.pointerType !== 'mouse') this.lastDevice = 'touch';   // any touch, on the stick's half or not: prompts follow it\n912:  label(a, device = this.lastDevice) {\n998:    if (code.startsWith('Pad')) { this.lastDevice = 'gamepad'; this.aimSource = 'pad'; }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DmdF1H5mxysfCdHgSkdSHC","permission_decisi