{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014izc8B3s4fjM9mBCNkjDd2","type":"tool_result","content":"836:- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\n837:- `E.tex.dirt(x, y, o = {})`: dirt, sand or snow: base color with soft noise and specks. o: { base, dark, light }\n838:- `E.tex.flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16)`: stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck}\n839:- `E.tex.grass(x, y, o = {})`: grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors\n840:- `E.tex.plain(x, y, o = {})`: plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount }\n841:- `E.tex.planks(x, y, o = {})`: wooden floor boards running along x. o: { base, dark, line }\n842:- `E.tex.water(x, y, o = {})`: water with static ripple lines (baked, so it does not move). o: { base, dark, light }\n16:- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n755:- `map.height(cx, cy)`: a cell's top: its wall's h, 0 on the floor, 1e9 outside the map (the height rules: E.HEIGHTS)\n756:- `map.heightAt(x, y)`: wall height at a world point (0 on the floor)\n770:- `map.standable(x, y, z, r = 5, step = HEIGHTS.step)`: can a body of radius r stand at (x, y) with its feet at z? Nothing under its footprint rises above z + step (it would collide), no blocked floor (water, lava) is under it at floor level, and\n17:- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n18:- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n19:- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n121:- `E.HEIGHTS: eye, chest, level, step`: the numbers of THE HEIGHT RULES, which collision, standing, sight, reach, navigation and drawing all read (API.md, \"Heights\", and the API index's head give \n180:- `E.sameLevel(a, b, tol = HEIGHTS.level)`: within tol (default E.HEIGHTS.level, 8) of the same height: sameLevel(hero, guard)\n514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n1050:- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track:\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: \n1642:- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"5fbaf959-245e-4d2f-a80f-07aeab17ef0c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:38:30.774Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"836:- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\n837:- `E.tex.dirt(x, y, o = {})`: dirt, sand or snow: base color with soft noise and specks. o: { base, dark, light }\n838:- `E.tex.flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16)`: stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck}\n839:- `E.tex.grass(x, y, o = {})`: grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors\n840:- `E.tex.plain(x, y, o = {})`: plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount }\n841:- `E.tex.planks(x, y, o = {})`: wooden floor boards running along x. o: { base, dark, line }\n842:- `E.tex.water(x, y, o = {})`: water with static ripple lines (baked, so it does not move). o: { base, dark, light }\n16:- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n755:- `map.height(cx, cy)`: a cell's top: its wall's h, 0 on the floor, 1e9 outside the map (the height rules: E.HEIGHTS)\n756:- `map.heightAt(x, y)`: wall height at a world point (0 on the floor)\n770:- `map.standable(x, y, z, r = 5, step = HEIGHTS.step)`: can a body of radius r stand at (x, y) with its feet at z? Nothing under its footprint rises above z + step (it would collide), no blocked floor (water, lava) is under it at floor level, and\n17:- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n18:- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n19:- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n121:- `E.HEIGHTS: eye, chest, level, step`: the numbers of THE HEIGHT RULES, which collision, standing, sight, reach, navigation and drawing all read (API.md, \"Heights\", and the API index's head give \n180:- `E.sameLevel(a, b, tol = HEIGHTS.level)`: within tol (default E.HEIGHTS.level, 8) of the same height: sameLevel(hero, guard)\n514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n1050:- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track:\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: \n1642:- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014izc8B3s4fjM9mBCNkjDd2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
