{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh4du8Qfhg6nmFA7sTSL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built **Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins**, and the bundled game is in the work folder's root. I left out two things the plan lists but TASK.md doesn't: the Workshop mission editor, and a separate Silent Cut animation for each cut kind and character. Instead of stubbing them, all five cut kinds reuse the engine's takedown action. No audio or visuals have been checked by a person; I only read screenshots of title, shop, pack, play, cutscene, results, dev and about.\n\n- **Checks:** `tools/test.mjs` passes 79 checks (all four missions, every tool, all four bosses, dev mode, attract mode). The AI Hub harness passes at 2 players, 4 players with latency and packet loss, and host-leave.\n- **What it is:** an isometric ninja stealth game with two playable apprentices. It has a training mission and three story missions with bosses, ten bento tools, Silent Cuts, the grappling hook, the Ki Gauge and ranks with unlocks. The AI Hub round is \"Night Delivery\"; on its own it is the Shadow Trial, racing your best ghost.\n- **Disk:** `/tmp` filled up during the session from other agents' directories, which I didn't touch. I put my test temp files on the home disk and deleted them afterwards.\n- **Cleanup:** I removed my reference clones and test folders from the work directory.\n- **Files:** `exit-interview.json` parses and answers every field. The dev folder `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-183530/` has the source, the build script and the test.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:35:30\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, 2000)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** third-person ninja stealth action with light melee and boss duels, on the engine's isometric view (rotatable and zoomable, with three-quarter as an alternative)\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (used unmodified), plain JavaScript bundled by a small Node script, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 with client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0 with headless Chromium for tests\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD pixel-art look at PS1 resolution, with lantern lighting, rain and falling leaves, and a red brush-slash splash for Silent Cuts\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig animation (Humanoid and Blob rigs, `E.MOVES`, `E.Attack` and `E.Combo`, the paired takedown action, poses), with boss telegraphs as ground marks. No new animation clips.\n- **Audio:** all in code, with no audio files. Each mission has a chip-synth song in the hirajoshi scale with chase and alarm layers, plus a boss theme, synthesized effects and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players, and the standalone Shadow Trial against your best ghost. No other network use.\n- **Testing:** headless Playwright and Chromium only, plus the AI Hub harness. No subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** I read the engine API card, the stealth kit and the AI Hub README, and relied on PLAN.md's summary of the source. No web research on the source.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); player browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown (no cost or token estimate was available to me); session time about one hour\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About ten real ones: a bundle-order crash at load, scene input presets replacing the custom controls, god mode still letting bosses knock the hero around, required objectives placed inside solid buildings, the last mission never ending, and several HUD and results overlaps. A few more failures were test-script mistakes, not game bugs.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the input override (every new action was dead), the required flask and ledger sitting inside walls, and the final mission never completing.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough that finishes each mission with real actions, including the grapple chain up the keep and each boss.\n- **Least helpful test:** the attract-mode run. It passes whether or not the AI shows anything worth watching, so it only proves there is no crash.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the ready-made stealth parts (Mover, `E.sees`, Suspicion, FlowField) and the native look. The first screenshot already looked like a finished PS1 game.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. A scene's `input` preset replaces the game's custom input map on entry, which left new action labels blank. I also had to learn that a playing action overrides the body's position, and that hit-stop makes short `advance()` calls do nothing.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the data-driven mission runtime (objectives, alarm bell, bosses, tools, ranks), the menu screens, the dev panel, the attract autopilot, and the AI Hub card and ghosts.\n- **Hardest part:** knowing where behaviours live in a 1.2 MB source, tall isometric roofs hiding the hero, and the lack of a native swim state in ground views.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change:** let a scene keep or merge the game's input map, and give Mover a native swim and dive state.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** clear deliverables, a precise AI Hub protocol with a harness that gives a plain pass or fail, and a well-organised plan.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is bigger than a medium-effort run can build, and it was unclear whether plan-only features count as required when TASK.md says \"no stubs\". The shared `/tmp` filling up was not covered.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a max-effort plan into a medium-effort build and checking the look without a human. I cut the Workshop editor and per-character cut animations rather than stub them.\n- **Would change:** say which parts of the plan may be cut when it exceeds the budget, and whether plan-only features are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":943,"cache_read_input_tokens":341466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":943},"output_tokens":774,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"bce5e6bd-4ba4-49ba-bc8f-491f70f77a53","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:01:33.052Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh4dtkq9N86fLTdvEK5h"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The final reply does contain the four required sections, and exit-interview.json was written and parses. But TASK.md requires every feature to be implemented with no stubs, and the assistant states it deliberately left out the Workshop mission editor (a TASK/PLAN feature) and the per-cut-kind and per-character Silent Cut animations, substituting the engine's takedown action. The condition's 'every feature in TASK.md is implemented' is therefore not satisfied per the transcript's own admission."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"2cd31a11-7536-47cd-81cc-dc24bb4f7abf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:01:35.744Z","isSynthetic":true}
