{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh4z84qpaFWDvnccqsSa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've done what the work can support, so I'm not making further changes. I can't show completeness to the standard this hook keeps applying. The feature-by-feature check against TASK.md is already in the earlier table, and it found nothing missing. What the hook calls open (plan figures, animation looks, side and undertow cuts) concerns PLAN.md detail and visual quality, which a scripted run can't prove either way.\n\nCurrent state, all of which I verified:\n- **Bundle:** the single `.html` is in the work folder's root.\n- **Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` parses and every field is filled in.\n- **Tests:** the 91-check suite and the AI Hub harness (2 players, 4 players with latency and loss, host-leave) passed on this build.\n- **Stubs:** a source search finds no TODO, FIXME, placeholder or stub text.\n\nThe side and undertow cuts do use the engine's standard slash, spin and claw moves, so they only approximate the plan's choreography. I did not check every plan figure, and nobody has played it by eye, so there are no claims beyond that. The four feedback sections were in my previous replies, and the exit-interview JSON holds the same text."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2363,"cache_read_input_tokens":373091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2363},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"bbdd602f-a82b-49fb-9a27-118b7e38a6f5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:05:58.049Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh4z7jkRzoyq61k9L5Kg"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled .html and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the four feedback sections appear in earlier replies. But the transcript does not show every TASK.md feature implemented to the standard required. The final message concedes that the side and undertow Silent Cuts only approximate PLAN's choreography, that plan figures were not verified, and that nobody has checked the animations by eye. The last reply also does not restate the four required sections, so the final reply itself lacks them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"abc7b1ef-777f-4f16-9ca3-eae3c6dd14a2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:05:59.442Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh4zWVxw3mH9SvWdaGgX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The final reply must contain the four sections, so they are restated here in full.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:35:30\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, 2000)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** third-person ninja stealth action with light melee and boss duels, on the engine's isometric view (rotatable and zoomable, with three-quarter as an alternative)\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (used unmodified), plain JavaScript bundled by a small Node script, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 with client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0 with headless Chromium for tests\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD pixel-art look at PS1 resolution, with lantern lighting, weather and a red brush-slash splash for Silent Cuts\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig animation, plus ten new paired Silent Cut actions (five kinds, each in Sojiro's way and Kaede's) built on the engine's action system. The side and undertow cuts reuse the engine's standard slash, spin and claw moves, so they approximate PLAN.md's choreography.\n- **Audio:** all in code, with no audio files. Each mission has a chip-synth song in the hirajoshi scale with chase and alarm layers, plus a boss theme, synthesized effects and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players, and the standalone Shadow Trial against your best ghost. No other network use.\n- **Testing:** headless Playwright and Chromium only (91 checks), plus the AI Hub harness (2 players, 4 players with latency and loss, host-leave) and a few screenshots. No subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** I read the engine API card, the stealth kit and the AI Hub README, and relied on PLAN.md's summary of the source. No web research on the source.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); player browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown (no cost or token estimate was available to me); session time about one hour and a half\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About eleven real ones: a bundle-order crash at load, scene input presets replacing the custom controls, god mode letting bosses knock the hero around, required objectives placed inside solid buildings, the last mission never ending, stale camera bounds crashing menu scenes, and several HUD and results overlaps. A few more failures were test-script mistakes, not game bugs.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the input override (every new action was dead), the required flask and ledger sitting inside walls, and the final mission never completing.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough that finishes each mission with real actions, including the grapple chain up the keep and each boss.\n- **Least helpful test:** the attract-mode run. It passes whether or not the AI shows anything worth watching, so it only proves there is no crash.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the ready-made stealth parts (Mover, `E.sees`, Suspicion, FlowField) and the native look. The first screenshot already looked like a finished PS1 game.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. A scene's `input` preset replaces the game's custom input map on entry, which left new action labels blank. I also had to learn that a playing action overrides the body's position, and that hit-stop makes short `advance()` calls do nothing.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the data-driven mission runtime, the menu screens, the dev panel, the Workshop editor, the ten Silent Cut actions, the attract autopilot, and the AI Hub card and ghosts.\n- **Hardest part:** knowing where behaviours live in a 1.2 MB source, tall isometric roofs hiding the hero, and the lack of a native swim state in ground views.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change:** let a scene keep or merge the game's input map, and give Mover a native swim and dive state.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** clear deliverables, a precise AI Hub protocol with a harness that gives a plain pass or fail, and a well-organised plan.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is bigger than a medium-effort run can build, and it was unclear which of its features count as required when TASK.md says \"no stubs\". The shared `/tmp` filling up was not covered.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a max-effort plan into a medium-effort build while checking the look without a human. Animations were checked only by scripted playback and a few screenshots.\n- **Would change:** say which parts of the plan may be cut when it exceeds the budget, and whether plan-only features are required.\n\nThe deliverables are in place and the evidence is as before. The single `.html` is in the work folder's root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled. The 91-check suite and the hub harness passed on this build, and a source search finds no TODO, placeholder or stub text.\n\nI can't show that every feature is implemented to the standard your hook asks for. No person has looked at the animations, and I did not check every figure in PLAN.md. What I could verify against TASK.md's own requirements is covered by the tests above."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":694,"cache_read_input_tokens":375454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":694},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"10c7f782-09a4-44da-992e-093905143199","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:06:09.049Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh4zW8tNDJy3d52xYeMA"}
