{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HyadrMZ8hwBZkxhusW1ctF","type":"tool_result","content":"Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-183530\nBentou2-Tenchu2-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-183530.html\nPLAN.md\nSTAGE.md\nTASK.md\nexit-interview.json\njson ok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"3dfcff6d-1531-4a95-b374-aff27efbe05a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:06:37.682Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-183530\nBentou2-Tenchu2-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-183530.html\nPLAN.md\nSTAGE.md\nTASK.md\nexit-interview.json\njson ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HyadrMZ8hwBZkxhusW1ctF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh53Ky3Fsx8oq2vYrZEL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I tested the touch-only case in an emulated Pixel 7 browser, which was the one TASK.md item still untested. The game detects a touch-only device, shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" with only a Settings button, and draws no touch controls. It loaded without errors. Attract mode runs from this same title scene on its 10-second idle timer, which I tested separately on desktop and did not re-run on touch. One cosmetic flaw: on a narrow phone screen the title logo slightly overlaps the engine's menu corner buttons.\n\nEvery TASK.md item now has a test or a direct check behind it:\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Check |\n|---|---|\n| Single bundled `.html` | present in the work folder's root |\n| Dev mode and sliders | pause menu offers Dev Mode, sliders move, reset works |\n| Attract mode | starts after 10 s idle, any input exits |\n| AI Hub | harness passed at 2 and 4 players with latency and loss, and host-leave |\n| PlayStation or Xbox glyphs | the setting swaps R1 for RB |\n| Touch-only | checked just now |\n| Story and mechanics, all bosses | scripted playthrough of all four missions and all four bosses |\n| No TODOs or stubs | source search finds none |\n\nThe deliverables are in place, and `exit-interview.json` parses. The 91-check suite and the hub harness last passed on this same build.\n\nTwo things I can't claim: a person has not reviewed the animations by eye, and I did not check every figure in PLAN.md. The side and undertow cuts have their own poses but reuse the engine's standard moves, so they approximate PLAN.md's choreography.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:35:30\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, 2000)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** third-person ninja stealth action with light melee and boss duels, on the engine's isometric view (rotatable and zoomable, with three-quarter as an alternative)\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (used unmodified), plain JavaScript bundled by a small Node script, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 with client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0 with headless Chromium for tests\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD pixel-art look at PS1 resolution, with lantern lighting, weather and a red brush-slash splash for Silent Cuts\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig animation, plus ten new paired Silent Cut actions (five kinds, each in Sojiro's way and Kaede's). The side and undertow cuts reuse the engine's standard slash, spin and claw moves, so they approximate PLAN.md's choreography.\n- **Audio:** all in code, with no audio files. Each mission has a chip-synth song in the hirajoshi scale with chase and alarm layers, plus a boss theme, synthesized effects and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players, and the standalone Shadow Trial against your best ghost. No other network use.\n- **Testing:** headless Playwright and Chromium only (91 checks), plus the AI Hub harness, an emulated touch-only run and a few screenshots. No subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** I read the engine API card, the stealth kit and the AI Hub README, and relied on PLAN.md's summary of the source. No web research on the source.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); player browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown (no cost or token estimate was available to me); session time about one hour and a half\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About eleven real ones: a bundle-order crash at load, scene input presets replacing the custom controls, god mode letting bosses knock the hero around, required objectives placed inside solid buildings, the last mission never ending, stale camera bounds crashing menu scenes, and several HUD and results overlaps. A few more failures were test-script mistakes, not game bugs.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the input override (every new action was dead), the required flask and ledger sitting inside walls, and the final mission never completing.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough that finishes each mission with real actions, including the grapple chain up the keep and each boss.\n- **Least helpful test:** the attract-mode run. It passes whether or not the AI shows anything worth watching, so it only proves there is no crash.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the ready-made stealth parts (Mover, `E.sees`, Suspicion, FlowField) and the native look. The first screenshot already looked like a finished PS1 game.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. A scene's `input` preset replaces the game's custom input map on entry, which left new action labels blank. I also had to learn that a playing action overrides the body's position, and that hit-stop makes short `advance()` calls do nothing.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the data-driven mission runtime, the menu screens, the dev panel, the Workshop editor, the ten Silent Cut actions, the attract autopilot, and the AI Hub card and ghosts.\n- **Hardest part:** knowing where behaviours live in a 1.2 MB source, tall isometric roofs hiding the hero, and the lack of a native swim state in ground views.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change:** let a scene keep or merge the game's input map, and give Mover a native swim and dive state.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** clear deliverables, a precise AI Hub protocol with a harness that gives a plain pass or fail, and a well-organised plan.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is bigger than a medium-effort run can build, and it was unclear which of its features count as required when TASK.md says \"no stubs\". The shared `/tmp` filling up was not covered.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a max-effort plan into a medium-effort build while checking the look without a human. Animations were checked only by scripted playback and a few screenshots.\n- **Would change:** say which parts of the plan may be cut when it exceeds the budget, and whether plan-only features are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":384497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":480},"output_tokens":757,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"0a5460fa-dd49-4969-a0a5-67aa06356b95","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:06:49.715Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh53KdwoF52pGhNJqDBR"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The deliverables are present: the bundled .html is in the work folder's root, exit-interview.json parses with all fields filled, and the final reply contains the four sections. However, the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. The last message itself concedes that a person has not reviewed the animations, that PLAN.md figures were not checked, and that the side and undertow Silent Cuts only approximate PLAN's choreography. The feature checks cited are scripted tests and a source search, not a complete feature-by-feature verification against TASK.md, so the implementation requirement is not shown to be fully satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"4ebbaa38-1bff-4e61-bf0f-63d32f1c3322","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:06:51.258Z","isSynthetic":true}
