{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh57RiR62bYTYi4fR3eh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The deliverables are complete and my evidence hasn't changed, so I'm making no further changes. The bundled `.html` is in the work folder's root, `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled, and the 91-check suite, the AI Hub harness and the touch-only check passed on this build. A source search finds no TODO or stub text.\n\nTwo things only a person can confirm: the animations by eye, and PLAN.md's figures. The side and undertow cuts reuse the engine's standard moves, so they approximate PLAN.md's choreography.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:35:30\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, 2000)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** third-person ninja stealth action with light melee and boss duels, on the engine's isometric view\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (unmodified), plain JavaScript bundled by a Node script, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 with client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD pixel-art look at PS1 resolution, with lantern lighting and weather\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig animation, plus ten new paired Silent Cut actions (five kinds, each in Sojiro's way and Kaede's)\n- **Audio:** all in code, with no audio files: chip-synth songs, synthesized effects and Animalese-style babble voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players, and the standalone Shadow Trial against your best ghost\n- **Testing:** headless Playwright only (91 checks), plus the AI Hub harness, a touch-only run and a few screenshots. No subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** I read the engine API card, the stealth kit and the AI Hub README; no web research on the source\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); player browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown (no cost or token estimate available); session time about one and a half hours\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About eleven real ones: a bundle-order crash at load, scene input presets replacing the custom controls, god mode letting bosses knock the hero around, required objectives placed inside solid buildings, the last mission never ending, stale camera bounds crashing menu scenes, and several HUD overlaps. A few more failures were test-script mistakes.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the input override, the flask and ledger sitting inside walls, and the final mission never completing.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough that finishes each mission with real actions, including the grapple chain up the keep and each boss.\n- **Least helpful test:** the attract-mode run, which only proves there is no crash.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the ready-made stealth parts (Mover, `E.sees`, Suspicion, FlowField) and the native look.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. A scene's `input` preset replaces the game's custom input map on entry. I also had to learn that a playing action overrides the body's position, and that hit-stop makes short `advance()` calls do nothing.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the data-driven mission runtime, the menus, the dev panel, the Workshop editor, the ten Silent Cut actions, the attract autopilot, and the AI Hub card and ghosts.\n- **Hardest part:** knowing where behaviours live in a 1.2 MB source, tall roofs hiding the hero, and no native swim state.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change:** let a scene keep or merge the game's input map, and give Mover a native swim and dive state.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** clear deliverables, a precise AI Hub protocol with a pass or fail harness, and a well-organised plan.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is bigger than a medium-effort run can build, and it was unclear which of its features count as required.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a max-effort plan into a medium-effort build while checking the look without a human.\n- **Would change:** say which parts of the plan may be cut when it exceeds the budget, and whether plan-only features are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2105,"cache_read_input_tokens":393427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2105},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43afccef-313a-4676-88e8-afa636ccfdd6","uuid":"a9983c51-7e7c-4280-be18-e1fc0c55f825","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:07:42.537Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh57RK7NqgSAK62crEGt"}
